 "note": "Black car with the neon STAR CHIP scheme. No near side-on photo of the left side: positions measured on the Getty / LAT photo 'Brands Hatch 26 August 1991, Dave Brodie' (2201200916, right side, mirrored and warped onto the model by the wheel centres and window corners); the left side is confirmed by the other LAT photo of that day (2201200818, front three-quarter, nose left: same number board, STAR CHIP on the front wing, lattice on the rear door, Brodie on the rear window) and the Thruxton TV graphic drawings. Same 4-door Sapphire shell as Gravett's car. Uncertain: the lattice and orange loops are drawn as a regular pattern (the real graphic is hand-drawn and irregular); star sizes and the exact stripe order on the bumpers are approximate; small stickers (Bilstein, Hoosier, the round logo) are partly unreadable. Wheels: dark centres with a polished lip, from on-track photos only (no photo of the car standing still). Logos (2026-11-16): the white Hoosier script on the wing is now the real logo. BILSTEIN fixed to dark letters on a white panel (LAT 2201200818, STR 4707); it stays lettering because the saved Bilstein logo is the blue box with the yellow disc, which the car does not show. STAR CHIP has no logo. The Hoosier on the front bumper (medium confidence) is not added. 2026-11-16: moved onto the new hand-traced Sapphire outline (same 4-door shell) by landmarks.",
